Chapter: E1000Swflag
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

Section: Fixtures

  dev-id-of : PciScanResult -> Integer
  dev-id-of (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> (d.pci-device-id)
      is None -> 0

  bring-up : PciScanResult -> E1000Device
  bring-up (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> e1000-init d
      is None -> e1000-absent

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  answered : Integer -> Text
  answered (v) = if v < 0 then "refused" else "answered"

Section: Entry

 THE PROBE IS AN MDIO READ, and it is chosen because it can say no. PHY ID1 is
 a fixed nonzero register, and `e1000-phy-read` answers negative one both for a
 PHY that never reports ready and for one that reports an error, so a refusal
 is distinguishable from a reading and cannot be mistaken for one.

 THE LADDER IS UNOWNED, OWNED, RELEASED, and the first and last rows are the
 kill states. A model that granted MDIO unconditionally would answer three
 times and fail rows 1 and 3; one that refused unconditionally would fail row
 2. Neither can pass all three (L-STATES, L-FALSIF).

 THE GRANT IS READ BACK, never inferred from the write, which is 82583V 4.5.2:
 the write either takes the bit or leaves it clear and never reports which.
 `acquire answers` is the function's verdict and `flag held` is the register,
 printed separately so a function that lies about its own success is visible.

 `e1000-pch-swflag-required` ships False, so `e1000-init` does not take the
 semaphore and the first row is the shipped state rather than a contrivance.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in let did = dev-id-of scan
    in let d = bring-up scan
    in let mmio = d.e-mmio
    in let unowned = e1000-phy-read mmio e1000-phy-id1
    in let got = e1000-swflag-acquire mmio e1000-swflag-fuel
    in let held = e1000-swflag-held mmio
    in let owned = e1000-phy-read mmio e1000-phy-id1
    in let rel = e1000-swflag-release mmio
    in let after = e1000-swflag-held mmio
    in let released = e1000-phy-read mmio e1000-phy-id1
    in act
      print-line-uni ("part is pch        : " & yn (e1000-pch-part did))
      print-line-uni ("shipped swflag step: " & yn e1000-pch-swflag-required)
      print-line-uni ("mdio unowned       : " & answered unowned)
      print-line-uni ("acquire answers    : " & show got)
      print-line-uni ("flag held          : " & yn held)
      print-line-uni ("mdio owned         : " & answered owned)
      print-line-uni ("flag after release : " & yn after)
      print-line-uni ("mdio released      : " & answered released)
    end
  end

